For the explicit $k=N=1$ stable scalar ADHM quotient and generic rotation weights with $\epsilon_1\epsilon_2\ne0$, extend the rotation torus by a flavor circle. Use natural units $c=\hbar=1$ and assign mass dimension one to the formal rotation weights $\epsilon_1,\epsilon_2$ and additive flavor mass $\widetilde m$. Let $q$ be a dimensionless formal variable marking instanton charge. The unique fixed point has tangent weights $\epsilon_1,\epsilon_2$, so the charge-one contribution of the top-Chern-class insertion for the inverse flavor line is
$$q I_{1,1}^{\mathrm{adj}}(\widetilde m)=q\frac{(\epsilon_1-\widetilde m)(\epsilon_2-\widetilde m)}{\epsilon_1\epsilon_2}.$$
The diagram shows the unique one-box partition, with the first coordinate horizontal for $B_1$ and the second vertical for $B_2$. This is a finite formal rank-one calculation only; the adopted S4 postulate in this batch is specifically $U(2)$.

~~~tikz
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=0.9cm]
  \draw[step=1,gray] (0,0) grid (1,1);
  \draw[fill=blue!20] (0,0) rectangle (1,1);
  \node at (0.5,0.5) {$Y_1=\square$};
  \draw[->] (0,0) -- (1.6,0) node[right] {$n_1\;(B_1)$};
  \draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,1.6) node[above] {$n_2\;(B_2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
~~~

Take $N=2$ and charge $k=1$ in the mass-inserted formal ADHM series. Use its dimensionless formal charge variable $q$; the equivariant weights $\epsilon_i,a_\alpha,\widetilde m$ have mass dimension one. Let $s=\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2$, $d=a_2-a_1$, and $\widetilde m=i m_E+s/2$ in the source's Euclidean mass convention. Exactly one box lies in either color, so the fixed-point tuples are $(\square,\varnothing)$ and $(\varnothing,\square)$. Their tangent characters and Euler classes are
$$\operatorname{ch}_T(T_{(\square,\varnothing)}X)=t_1+t_2+\frac{e_2}{e_1}+t_1t_2\frac{e_1}{e_2}$$
$$E_1=\epsilon_1\epsilon_2d(s-d),\qquad N_1=(\epsilon_1-\widetilde m)(\epsilon_2-\widetilde m)(d-\widetilde m)(s-d-\widetilde m)$$
$$\operatorname{ch}_T(T_{(\varnothing,\square)}X)=t_1+t_2+\frac{e_1}{e_2}+t_1t_2\frac{e_2}{e_1}$$
$$E_2=-\epsilon_1\epsilon_2d(s+d),\qquad N_2=(\epsilon_1-\widetilde m)(\epsilon_2-\widetilde m)(-d-\widetilde m)(s+d-\widetilde m).$$
For generic weights satisfying $\epsilon_1\epsilon_2d(s-d)(s+d)\ne0$, the coefficient of $q$ is
$$\frac{N_1}{E_1}+\frac{N_2}{E_2}=\frac{2(\epsilon_1-\widetilde m)(\epsilon_2-\widetilde m)(\widetilde m^2-\widetilde m s+s^2-d^2)}{\epsilon_1\epsilon_2(s^2-d^2)}.$$
For the adopted $S^4_r$ model, set $\epsilon_1=\epsilon_2=r^{-1}$ and $\widetilde m=i m_E+r^{-1}$. At $m_E=0$ the displayed one-instanton coefficient vanishes because its first two numerator factors are zero; this is only the degree-one check of the N=4 massless limit.

The diagram places the single box in each of the two possible framing colors. The first coordinate is horizontal and the second vertical.

